{
  "id": "ml-inference-route-registration-backend-auto-discovery-and-f",
  "title": "ml_inference route registration: backend auto-discovery and frontend scene URL",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "How are ml_inference routes registered?",
    "Do I need to edit rest_router.py when adding a product API?",
    "Where is the decision playground URL mapped to a scene?"
  ],
  "body": "Backend:\n1. products/ml_inference/backend/routes.py:register_routes registers DecisionViewSet on routers.projects (path `ml_inference/decisions`, basename `project_ml_inference_decisions`, parent lookup [\"team_id\"]).\n2. posthog/api/rest_router.py, \"Product route auto-discovery\" loop at bottom: load_product_modules(\"routes\") then calls each `register_routes(routers)`. No per-product edit there. Registry type is documented in posthog/api/routing.py (RouterRegistry).\n3. Discovery is via INSTALLED_APPS: products.ml_inference.backend.apps.MlInferenceConfig is listed in posthog/settings/web.py.\nFrontend (separate): products/ml_inference/manifest.tsx maps `/ml-inference/decisions` to the DecisionPlayground scene; frontend/src/productScenes.tsx lazy-imports it.\nThe loop is eager at ROOT_URLCONF import, not AppConfig.ready() (comment in rest_router.py).",
